          "title": "Blackjack Switch",
          "subtitle": "Gambling",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Blackjack Switch is a patented casino blackjack variant where each betting position receives two hands and may switch the second cards between them."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Invented by Geoff Hall and patented in 2009 as a casino table-game variant of blackjack."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "1-7 against dealer players use the table arrangement described for Blackjack Switch."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Multiple standard 52-card decks"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Multiple standard 52-card decks, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Each player position receives two blackjack hands against the dealer before the switch decision is offered."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
